Package: mappingAS
Type: Package
Title: Range Metrics (EOO/AOO) and MapBiomas Habitat Conversion for Species Assessment
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Seu", "Nome", email = "voce@exemplo.org", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A GeoCat-style toolkit for IUCN Red List Criterion B screening that
    accepts species occurrence points from XLSX, CSV, or shapefile inputs,
    computes Extent of Occurrence (EOO, minimum convex polygon) and Area of
    Occupancy (AOO, 2x2 km grid), and quantifies the percentage of converted
    (anthropic) versus remaining natural habitat inside both the EOO and the AOO
    using the most recent MapBiomas land-use/land-cover collection. Land cover
    can be read either locally (windowed reads from the national GeoTIFF, no
    Google Earth Engine account required) or via Google Earth Engine (for very
    large ranges). Includes a Shiny application for interactive, friendly use.
